claim("gallbladder-filling-versus-emptying","Gallbladder-filling scintigraphy evaluates cystic-duct patency, whereas stimulated ejection fraction evaluates gallbladder emptying.",["snm-hida","wses"],"evaluation","One technique-specific guideline plus an independent acute-disease guideline. Normal ultrasound wall/fluid components do not exclude acute disease; a universal HIDA-over-every-CT/MRI ranking is not asserted.");
claim("mixed-discharge-medication","Metoclopramide can increase prolactin and produce galactorrhea.",["reglan-label"],"presentation","Primary regulatory label only for this drug fact; no dose, timing or causation of a focal breast lesion claimed. Separate existing discharge claims support assessment of spontaneous unilateral episodes.");
claim("mixed-discharge-local-assessment","Spontaneous unilateral nipple discharge warrants breast-local assessment rather than being explained away by expressed bilateral secretion.",["pitarch"],"evaluation","Application synthesized from the separate pattern definitions in one open review, not a reported mixed-phenotype trial. Color alone is not a malignancy diagnosis; the medication-associated component can coexist.");
claim("initial-breast-pathway","In women over 40 with a pathologic discharge pattern, initial mammography is generally combined with ultrasound; MRI has a subsequent problem-solving role.",["pitarch"],"evaluation","One current open imaging review, cross-checked against retained project discharge-imaging evidence. The exact age boundary is supported by the source; every supplied female profile is above it. Local imaging suitability remains clinician review.");
claim("boosted-midazolam-routes","Oral midazolam is contraindicated with ritonavir-boosted protease-inhibitor therapy.",["nysdoh-hiv"],"safety_boundary","One adequately retrieved current guideline for this added interaction fact; NIH direct table returned 403 and is not counted as independent verification.");
claim("boosted-parenteral-titration","Parenteral midazolam may be considered with boosted protease inhibitors in an appropriately monitored setting, with dose reduction considered particularly for repeated doses.",["nysdoh-hiv"],"management","One verified current guideline. No exact dose, mandatory universal reduction, unsupervised administration or washout interval authored; anesthesia/HIV coordination required.");
claim("art-continuity","Avoid uncoordinated perioperative ART interruption; consult the HIV team when interruption cannot be avoided.",["nysdoh-hiv"],"management","One verified current guideline; administration feasibility and individual interactions still require clinical review. The existing named-regimen claim independently verifies the four-drug combination.");
claim("pressure-not-peristalsis","Simultaneous panesophageal pressurization is not preserved propagated peristalsis when classifying achalasia.",["chicago","seoul"]);
claim("primary-position-achalasia","Abnormal median IRP in the primary test position with absent peristalsis can establish achalasia; abnormal IRP in both positions is not required as it is for an EGJOO pattern.",["chicago"],"evaluation","Single primary classification consensus for the exact positional distinction; ten primary-position swallows and protocol adequacy require clinical confirmation. No device-specific IRP threshold invented.");
claim("spastic-achalasia","Premature or failed rather than normally peristaltic swallows with abnormal junction relaxation support a spastic achalasia pattern.",["chicago","seoul"],"evaluation","The constructed case uses most premature swallows and remaining failed swallows; no subtype label is asked. Technical adequacy, latency reference and opioid effects require review.");
claim("failed-contraction-threshold","Chicago v4.0 classifies DCI below 100 mmHg.s.cm as failed contraction.",["chicago"],"definition","The exact cutoff is explicitly supported by the consensus. B04's 30-80 readings are synthetic examples inside that range, not an invented normal threshold or measured patient dataset.");
claim("esophageal-physiology-sequence","High-resolution manometry supplies esophageal motor classification when persistent obstructive swallowing symptoms remain after structural evaluation.",["chicago","seoul"],"evaluation","FLIP can complement inconclusive studies or be used in selected circumstances; it is not declared useless. No later pressure result is used to justify the earlier task.");
claim("groin-initial-dynamic-assessment","Ultrasound is an initial imaging approach for suspected groin hernia when examination does not establish the diagnosis.",["hernia2018","hernia2023"],"evaluation","MRI can be appropriate after unresolved assessment; the case establishes first imaging and an intermittent lump, without an availability cue.");
claim("symptomatic-groin-planning","Activity-limiting symptoms from an inguinal hernia favor discussion of elective repair rather than treating the patient as an asymptomatic watchful-waiting candidate.",["hernia2018","hernia2023"],"management","Risk, preferences and surgical assessment remain necessary; no compulsory operation, emergency state or outcome probability asserted.");
claim("papillary-cytology-regional-survey","Malignant thyroid cytology warrants preoperative ultrasound assessment of central and lateral cervical nodal compartments.",["ata2025"],"evaluation","Current primary guideline supports the initial survey; additional CT/MRI or sampling can be appropriate for extensive/invasive or sonographically suspicious disease. No node-size threshold authored.");
claim("papillary-cytology-pattern","Papillary groups with nuclear grooves and intranuclear cytoplasmic inclusions support a papillary thyroid carcinoma interpretation.",["ptc-cytology"],"evaluation","A groove alone is insufficient; integrated architecture/nuclei and cytopathologist review are required. No histologic subtype or absolute specificity is taught.");
claim("melanoma-integrated-node-staging","Clinically node-negative invasive melanoma in the supplied greater-than-1-mm range calls for sentinel-node staging consideration; reassuring ultrasound does not replace microscopic nodal staging.",["eado2024","nci-melanoma"],"management","Existing synthetic thickness values are retained. No fixed metastatic probability or survival benefit asserted; subtype and patient suitability remain clinician review.");
claim("melanoma-diagnostic-sampling","When feasible, complete diagnostic removal of a suspicious melanocytic lesion supports assessment of its architecture and invasion depth.",["eado2024","nci-melanoma"],"evaluation","The offered tangential option is explicitly limited to papillary dermis; this does not condemn every shave or require excision in anatomically unsuitable lesions.");
claim("malignant-polyp-adverse-features","Adverse invasive-polyp histology or incomplete resection can warrant oncologic regional resection despite a clear-looking scar.",["ascrs-colon"],"management","One verified primary guideline for this added scope: lymphovascular invasion, poor differentiation, involved deep margin and fragmentation are separately constructed case findings. Individual pedunculated/sessile risk and operative fitness require review; normal CT nodes do not prove microscopic negativity.");
claim("colon-systemic-staging","Chest, abdominal and pelvic CT is a standard initial colon-cancer staging pathway; routine PET-CT is not its automatic replacement.",["ascrs-colon"],"evaluation","Single retrieved guideline. Chest CT plus abdominal MRI is also an accepted pathway and is deliberately not offered as wrong; chest radiography is not equivalent thoracic staging. Contrast suitability assumed, not guaranteed.");
claim("sarcoma-viable-biopsy-target","Image-guided core sampling of a heterogeneous soft-tissue tumor should target viable tumor identified with enhancement or vascularity.",["essr2015-target","seom2024"],"evaluation","Exact targeting is directly supported by older primary technique guidance; current society guidance corroborates planned image-guided core biopsy. No diagnostic certainty from MRI alone, invented needle size or tract rule added.");
claim("sarcoma-local-imaging","MRI is the preferred local characterization/staging study for a deep or indeterminate limb soft-tissue mass before planned biopsy.",["essr2023","seom2024"],"evaluation","CT is useful in selected circumstances; ultrasound can triage accessible lesions. The supplied prior ultrasound establishes deep extent, rather than merely a lesion beneath skin.");
claim("subepithelial-integrated-pattern","A homogeneous bright submucosal lesion with a yellow deformable endoscopic appearance supports lipoma characterization.",["esge-sel2022"],"evaluation","One primary guideline for the added raw EUS detail; existing lipoma evidence separately supports no directed follow-up when confidently characterized and asymptomatic. Not all SELs can be diagnosed from EUS alone.");
claim("gastric-depth-nodes-organ-plan","A gastric primary extending into muscularis propria falls outside the early T1 nodal-dissection scope and supports a D2 framework in the represented operative plan.",["jgca2021","korean-gastric"],"management","The synthetic wall-layer observation must be checked by Melissa. No exact nodal station algorithm or disputed JGCA2025 hilar recommendation is used.");
claim("gastric-spleen-preservation","Prophylactic splenectomy is not routine for the represented proximal gastric cancer without greater-curvature or splenic invasion.",["korean-gastric","jgca2021"],"management","The separate contradictory English JGCA2025 hilar statement remains withheld. Direct invasion or therapeutic nodal indications can change scope; the case's fat plane is not proof against every microscopic extension.");
claim("gastric-lineage-not-classification","CD20 establishes B-cell lineage but is insufficient without representative morphology and ancillary assessment to classify gastric MALT lymphoma.",["bsh-mzl","malt2023"],"evaluation","Repeat representative biopsies are warranted for the constructed crushed, architecture-poor sample. Clonality alone can occur in reactive inflammation and does not resolve every lymphoma subtype.");
claim("gastric-malt-response-assessment","Histologic gastric response assessment is needed after H. pylori-directed treatment of gastric MALT lymphoma; symptoms alone do not establish remission.",["bsh-mzl","malt2023"],"management","No eradication regimen, exact follow-up interval, universal response probability or automatic salvage rule authored.");
claim("gastric-small-b-cell-differential","Gastric small B-cell infiltration with gland involvement and a CD20/CD79a-positive, CD5/CD10/cyclin-D1-negative profile supports MALT lymphoma in integrated pathology review.",["bsh-mzl","malt2023"],"evaluation","Markers have exceptions; this is not a unique single-stain rule, and lymphoma classification requires morphology, clinical context and expert review.");
claim("null-test-versus-protocol-magnitude","Testing against no effect and evaluating a prespecified meaningful effect or equivalence margin are different statistical questions.",["nist-p","nist-ci","lakens2017"],"definition","B26/B27/B31/B39 numbers, targets and intervals are constructed protocol inputs, not clinical thresholds or observed treatment effects. TOST .05 uses a 90% CI, not a substituted 95% CI; arithmetic/rounding is separately validated.");
claim("odds-to-risk-conversion","For a fixed covariate profile, multiply baseline odds by the conditional odds ratio, then convert resulting odds to risk as odds/(1+odds).",["dhsc-odds"],"definition","Algebraic derivation from definitions, not a causal/marginal prediction. With baseline .40 and OR .60 the risk is 2/7, approximately 29%; all values are fictional inputs.");
claim("relative-to-absolute-interval","With a fixed reference risk, a risk-ratio interval transforms to a risk-difference interval by multiplying each endpoint by that risk and subtracting it.",["dhsc-odds","nist-ci"],"definition","Derived algebra on fictional inputs: .20*(.40-1)=-.12 and .20*(1.20-1)=.04. A reference-risk uncertainty distribution is not supplied or assumed; intervals are not hard bounds on truth.");
claim("sedation-supported-discharge","After IV sedation, discharge planning includes assessed recovery and responsible adult support, not a driver-only transport booking.",["bsg-sedation"],"disposition","One current specialist guideline plus retained existing local discharge advice. Local approved escort pathways may differ; no taxi-only shortcut, fixed recovery duration or blanket rule for unsedated/nitrous procedures taught.");
claim("sedation-after-reversal","Re-sedation can follow flumazenil reversal of midazolam, so apparent immediate recovery does not remove the need for further monitoring.",["bsg-sedation"],"safety_boundary","One primary specialist guideline. No exact observation period or dose authored; prior benzodiazepine/opioid exposure and individual risk require review.");
claim("pancreatic-contrast-characterization","Pre-drainage cross-sectional imaging of a pancreatic fluid collection assesses wall, contents, adjacent organs and vessels.",["ksge"],"evaluation","CT/MRCP and EUS play complementary roles. The item compares specified CT contrast protocols, not CT against a falsely invalid MRI pathway; actual vascular and contrast suitability remain review requirements.");
claim("collection-symptom-attribution","Persistent attributable symptoms or obstruction can warrant drainage assessment of a walled pancreatic fluid collection.",["ksge"],"management","One verified guideline for this added application. Referral is for access/expertise and symptom attribution assessment, not immediate puncture; no size-only cutoff, exact elapsed time or invented vessel clearance authored.");
claim("pdsa-outcome-balancing-adaptation","Improvement-cycle decisions should consider whether process changes improve the intended outcome and add burden, then use the findings to plan the next test.",["ahrq-pdca","ahrq-metrics"],"management","B36 is a fictional process pilot, not patient trial evidence or question correctness analytics. The data favor adapting the form over rollout or training-only repetition; no universal abandon threshold taught.");
claim("ibc-core-versus-adjunctive-skin","Breast core tissue confirms invasive carcinoma in a suspected inflammatory breast cancer presentation; skin punch can add dermal information but does not replace that confirmation.",["ibc-consensus","nci-ibc"],"evaluation","Existing primary-consensus claim retained; dermal emboli are not required. The poorly informative prior aspirate motivates a tissue core, and staging is conditional on confirmation, preserving the existing external-service bundle.");
claim("ibc-response-local-treatment","Clinical response to neoadjuvant treatment does not by itself remove the mastectomy and regional radiation components of the represented operable stage III inflammatory breast cancer pathway.",["nci-ibc-treatment","ago2024"],"management","Conditional future planning, not a claim that systemic therapy occurred during biopsy wait; individual operability and response require review. No modern non-IBC de-escalation rule is extrapolated.");
claim("ulcer-local-modality-choice","A nonbleeding ulcer vessel can receive mechanical or contact-thermal hemostasis; epinephrine alone is inadequate, and topical agents are not routine sole initial therapy for that finding.",["esge-ulcer"],"management","Current specific guideline only for the new modality comparison; retained ACG evidence independently supports hemostasis indication. Powder can be appropriate rescue/temporizing therapy; after the failed clip the selected contact treatment supplements epinephrine rather than repeating monotherapy. No dose or universal rescue sequence authored.");
for(const c of claims)for(const id of c.sourceIds){const s=sources.find(s=>s.id===id);if(!s)throw Error(id);s.evidenceClaimIds.push(c.id);}
